      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, Reviewer 3's critique regarding the fixed seed in Monte Carlo simulations is a significant methodological flaw that typically precludes publication in high-impact journals. Scientific consensus generally requires demonstrating that results are robust to initial conditions; relying on a single seed risks proving an artifact rather than a universal physical property. In a research context involving quantum lattices, this statistical validity issue is severe enough to demand a major revision or re-analysis before the work is considered ready for release. While an erratum could address it post-publication, the current state of the manuscript undermines its core claim of establishing true stability thresholds, making immediate rejection or substantial revision the standard course of action.",
